<title>HONG KONG: Johnson buys back US$10 mln convertibles.</title>
<headline>Johnson buys back US$10 mln convertibles.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Johnson Electric Holdings Ltd on Monday said it had bought back US$10 million of its original US$150 million issue of 4.5 percent convertible bonds due 2000.</p>
<p>The company said in an announcement released through the stock exchange, that it had made the repurchase on January 31.  </p>
<p>The company issued the bonds, approximately equal to HK$1,159 million, in May 1993.</p>
<p>Johnson shares were trading HK$0.05 higher at HK$23.45 in early Monday morning trade.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6933</p>
